---
// /privacy — polityka prywatności (RODO/GDPR). Administrator = Kacper Mioduszewski
// jako osoba fizyczna (decyzja 16.07.2026: bez zawieszonej działalności).
// Aktualizować przy każdej zmianie procesorów (hosting, mail, kalendarz, analityka).
import VariantLayout from '../layouts/VariantLayout.astro';
const updated = '11 August 2026';
---

<VariantLayout
  title="Privacy policy · mioduszewsky"
  bg="#f8f9f2"
  fg="#000000"
  switcher={false}
  robots="index, follow"
  description="How mioduszewsky.com handles your data under GDPR."
>
  <main class="doc">
    <header class="doc-nav">
      <a class="mark" href="/" aria-label="mioduszewsky — back home">
        <video autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="auto" aria-hidden="true" poster="/logo3d/logo-nav-poster.webp">
          <source src="/logo3d/logo-nav.mp4" type="video/mp4;codecs=hvc1" />
          <source src="/logo3d/logo-nav.webm" type="video/webm" />
        </video>
      </a>
      <a class="back" href="/">← Back</a>
    </header>

    <article class="doc-body">
      <p class="label">( Legal )</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="upd">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data I collect through
        <strong>mioduszewsky.com</strong>, why, and what rights you have. It follows
        the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / RODO).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is <strong>Kacper Mioduszewski</strong>, a private
        individual, ul. Fromborska 66, 54-111 Wrocław, Poland. Contact:
        <a href="mailto:kacper@mioduszewsky.com">kacper@mioduszewsky.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What data I collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form</strong> — your name, email address and the content of
          your message. Used only to reply to your enquiry and, if relevant, to take
          steps toward working together.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking a call</strong> — if you schedule a call, the booking is
          handled by Google (Google Calendar appointment scheduling). Google receives
          your name, email and any details you provide, to confirm the meeting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic usage analytics</strong> — anonymous, aggregated statistics about
          page visits (which pages, rough referrer, device type). This is
          <strong>cookieless</strong> and does not identify you individually. Always on,
          no consent needed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional product analytics and ad conversion tracking</strong> —
          PostHog (to understand how people use the site), Google Analytics / Google
          Ads conversion tracking and the Meta Pixel (to measure whether paid ads lead
          to real enquiries). These only run <strong>after you accept the cookie
          banner</strong> — see section 6.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional session recordings</strong> — if you accept the cookie
          banner, PostHog also records your visit: the pages you move through, clicks,
          scrolling and mouse movement, played back later as a video-like replay. I use
          this to find out where the site confuses people. <strong>Anything you type
          into a form field is masked and never recorded</strong>, passwords included.
          Recordings are automatically deleted after 30 days. This does not run if you
          reject the banner.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your <strong>consent</strong> for processing the contact form (Art. 6(1)(a)) — given by ticking the consent box.</li>
        <li>Your <strong>consent</strong> for PostHog, Google and Meta analytics/ad tracking (Art. 6(1)(a)) — given by accepting the cookie banner. Nothing loads before that.</li>
        <li>Your <strong>consent</strong> for session recordings (Art. 6(1)(a)) — the same banner. Reject it, or simply do not accept, and nothing is recorded.</li>
        <li>Taking <strong>steps at your request before entering a contract</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b)).</li>
        <li>My <strong>legitimate interest</strong> in understanding, in aggregate, how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f)) — for the cookieless basic analytics only.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Who processes your data on my behalf</h2>
      <p>I use a small number of trusted service providers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> — website hosting and cookieless Web Analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS SES)</strong> — delivery of contact-form emails. Data is processed in the EU (Frankfurt, eu-central-1).</li>
        <li><strong>Google (Google Workspace)</strong> — my email inbox and, if you book a call, the appointment scheduling.</li>
        <li><strong>PostHog</strong> (EU servers) — product analytics and session recordings, only after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics / Google Ads</strong> — traffic and ad-conversion measurement, only after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
        <li><strong>Meta Platforms Ireland</strong> — the Meta Pixel, used to measure whether paid ads lead to real enquiries, only after you accept the cookie banner.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some providers are based outside the EU. Where that applies, transfers rely on
        the EU Standard Contractual Clauses or an equivalent safeguard.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Contact messages are kept for as long as needed to handle your enquiry and any
        resulting collaboration, and then for a reasonable period in case of follow-up.
        You can ask me to delete them sooner at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Session recordings are deleted automatically after 30 days.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>mioduszewsky.com itself sets no cookies by default.</strong> My basic
        analytics are cookieless and do not identify you.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a <strong>cookie banner</strong> is shown on the site, it is asking your
        consent to run two additional tools: <strong>PostHog</strong> (product
        analytics <strong>and session recordings</strong>, described in section 2) and
        <strong>Google Analytics / Google Ads</strong> (traffic and
        ad-conversion measurement). Neither loads before you click “Accept” — if you
        click “Reject”, or never see a banner because these tools are not active yet,
        none of this runs and no related cookie is set. Your choice is remembered on
        this device so you are not asked again.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <strong>booking calendar on the /contact page</strong> is provided by
        Google, and once shown it sets a cookie (Google's <code>NID</code>) needed to
        run that widget. If you have already accepted the cookie banner, the calendar
        loads automatically; otherwise it only loads after you click “Show calendar”.
        If you would rather not, you can always book by emailing
        <a href="mailto:kacper@mioduszewsky.com">kacper@mioduszewsky.com</a> instead.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under GDPR you can, at any time:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access your data and get a copy,</li>
        <li>correct or update it,</li>
        <li>ask for it to be deleted,</li>
        <li>restrict or object to processing,</li>
        <li>withdraw consent (without affecting past processing),</li>
        <li>lodge a complaint with the Polish supervisory authority (UODO, <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">uodo.gov.pl</a>).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:kacper@mioduszewsky.com">kacper@mioduszewsky.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the “last updated” date above will change too.</p>
    </article>

    <footer class="doc-foot">
      <span>© 2026 mioduszewsky</span>
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <style>
    @font-face { font-family: 'NohemiV'; src: url('/fonts/Nohemi-Variable.woff2') format('woff2'); font-weight: 100 900; font-display: swap; }
    @font-face { font-family: 'GeneralSansV'; src: url('/fonts/GeneralSans-Variable.woff2') format('woff2'); font-weight: 200 700; font-display: swap; }

    .doc {
      --ink:#000; --ivory:#f8f9f2; --dim:#8b8677; --blue:#0522ff;
      font-family:'GeneralSansV',sans-serif; background:var(--ivory); color:var(--ink);
      min-height:100svh; padding:0 6vw 6vh; display:flex; flex-direction:column;
    }
    .doc-nav { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; padding:20px 0; }
    /* logotyp ma proporcje ~3.6:1, wiec kwadratowy kontener + object-fit:contain
       scisnal go do ~15px wysokosci. Wysokosc steruje, szerokosc sie dostosowuje,
       tak jak w nawigacji na stronie glownej. */
    .doc-nav .mark { display:block; }
    .doc-nav .mark video { height:clamp(40px,3.4vw,54px); width:auto; display:block; }
    .back { text-decoration:none; color:var(--ink); font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.16em; text-transform:uppercase; }
    .back:hover { color:var(--blue); }
    .label { font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.26em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--dim); }
    .doc-body { max-width:66ch; margin:5vh auto; width:100%; }
    .doc-body h1 { font-family:'NohemiV',sans-serif; font-weight:520; letter-spacing:-0.025em; font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.6rem); margin:1rem 0 0.4rem; }
    .upd { color:var(--dim); font-size:13px; margin-bottom:2.5rem; }
    .doc-body h2 { font-family:'NohemiV',sans-serif; font-weight:540; letter-spacing:-0.015em; font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.5rem); margin:2.4rem 0 0.8rem; }
    .doc-body p, .doc-body li { font-size:16px; line-height:1.7; color:#3a382f; }
    .doc-body ul { margin:0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.2rem; }
    .doc-body li { margin-bottom:0.5rem; }
    .doc-body a { color:var(--blue); }
    .doc-foot { display:flex; gap:1.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:auto; padding-top:6vh; font-size:12px; color:var(--dim); letter-spacing:0.04em; }
    .doc-foot a { color:var(--dim); text-decoration:none; }
    .doc-foot a:hover { color:var(--ink); }
  </style>
</VariantLayout>
